      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 18 August 2026 — Cardrona is open today with a fresh top-up of snow overnight, and conditions are looking superb after the snowmaking and grooming teams made the most of the cold weather through the night. It's a cold one today with strong southwest winds, so grab an extra layer — there's a cloud cap sitting over the mountain at the moment, with fingers crossed for a clearance. It's currently -2 degrees, with wind around 23km/h and gusts to 40. Main Basin lifts get going from 8:30am, with Captains, T-Bar, Soho and Willows following from 9am. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express and Valley View round out the rest of the open lifts. The Wells Pipe Platter is closed, and up top, Mt Cardrona, Arcadia Chutes and the Summit terrain remain on hold, along with Big Bucks in the park. Chains must always be carried, and there's an active road hazard advisory on the Cardrona and Treble Cone access roads worth checking before heading up. Carpark A is full, but B, C, The Yard, Valley View and The Pines all still have space. If you're after lunch, locals avoid the 1pm rush — grab a snack outside peak times, or book a table at The Mezz. Anyone with a season's pass will need a photo on their profile this year; pop into Guest Services if you're not sure whether yours is sorted.",
