      "summary": ": Today at Treble Cone 18 August 2026 — Mid-season goodness continues at Treble Cone — the groomers have done their thing, so it's your turn now. It's a clear winter morning, with another cold night leaving crisp conditions and a fresh groomed surface to start the day. There's a cool southerly up top, so dress warm for the wind chill, especially out in The Saddle. It's currently -1 degree, with wind around 18km/h and gusts to 32. Home Basin opens at 8:30am and Saddle Basin at 9am, with the Home Basin Express, Saddle Quad and Beginner Platter running. Triple Treat, Main Street, Big Skite, Rafill's Run, Pete's Treat, High Street and Saddle Track are all groomed and open. The Summit and Motatapu Chutes are open, and Matukituki is open too, with a high traverse out recommended. If you're new to the mountain, the Ski School team can help you find your feet on the Beginner Platter. All vehicles must carry chains, and there's an active road hazard advisory on the Cardrona and Treble Cone access roads worth checking before heading up — carpooling or the free road shuttle are good options. It's a big week on the mountain, with the Freeride World Tour 2-Star Qualifier kicking off tomorrow, the Treble Cone Interfields Ski Race this Saturday, and Atomic Rise & Shine Round 3 on Sunday.",
